Oplus Zstd crypto backend
========================

Imported from the user-supplied zstd_o.zip on 2026-10-31. The bundled
Zstandard library identifies itself as 1.4.10. The crypto backend registers
zstdn_o at compression level 1, alongside the existing zstd algorithm.

Integration changes:
- Build through CONFIG_CRYPTO_ZSTDN and list zstdn_o in zram's algorithms.
- Include linux/types.h explicitly for the 4.14 size_t definition.
- Force-include namespace.h so the library's global symbols do not collide
  with the existing Zstd, entropy coding, and xxhash implementations.
- Report successful registration only if both crypto registrations succeed.

namespace.h lists all global definitions in crypto_zstdn_o.o, as reported by
nm -g --defined-only. Regenerate and inspect that list whenever updating the
bundled sources. Do not prefix external kernel references.

The userspace zram setup chooses the compression algorithm before setting
disksize. Enabling this backend does not change zram's default compressor.

Do not treat zstdn_o as interchangeable with the legacy zstd backend. Device
testing found cross-decoding failures in both directions (7 of 18 input
cases each). Keep the distinct algorithm name and reset/reinitialize zram
before selecting it; never relabel existing compressed data.
